  ('solden-austria', '01F', 'Sölden', 'Austria', 'Two glaciers, a fleet of 3,000-metre peaks, the World', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Austria', '{"ski","adventure","entertainment","wellness","culinary","family"}', '{"alpine","dramatic","festive"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["BIG3 = three 3,000 m peaks (Gaislachkogl 3,058 m, Tiefenbachkogl 3,250 m, Schwarze Schneide 3,340 m high point) linked by viewing platforms; Otztal, Tirol; village ~1,368 m","~145 km pistes (76 easy/40 int/29 diff) + ski routes; 31 lifts; base ~1,350 m to 3,340 m; ~1,990 m vertical (among Austria''s biggest)","Two glaciers (Rettenbach + Tiefenbach) via one of Europe''s highest paved roads = Oct-May snow-sure season","FIS Alpine Ski World Cup OPENER on the Rettenbach glacier every late Oct (2025/26 opened 26 Oct 2025, men''s GS Odermatt)","James Bond Spectre (2015) filmed here; 007 Elements installation at Gaislachkogl summit; ice Q restaurant = the film''s ''Hoffler Klinik''","Adult day pass ~EUR 83; Snow Card Tirol + Otztal Superskicard (links Obergurgl-Hochgurgl); Epic Pass listing on skiresort.info UNVERIFIED (not asserted); no Ikon","Das Central = 5-star (Michelin KEY = hotel award NOT restaurant star; G&M 4 toques/97; Summit Spa ~2,000 m2); Hotel Bergland = 5-star design (Sky SPA ~2,200 m2; Spectre set)","Wildspitze (3,768 m), Tyrol''s highest peak, in the municipality - a classic ski-touring/mountaineering objective","Events: FIS World Cup opener, Hannibal glacier spectacle (Rettenbach), Electric Mountain Festival; lively apres/nightlife","Reached via Otztal Bahnhof (Innsbruck ~85-90 km) + valley bus; heli-skiing NOT available (Austria permits it only at Vorarlberg/Lech-Zurs sites)","~1,990 m vertical (base ~1,350 m to Schwarze Schneide 3,340 m) - among the biggest verticals in Austria","Otztal Glacier Road = among Europe''s highest paved roads, the access route to the Rettenbach/Tiefenbach glaciers","Hannibal = large 